## Incoming manus-parity report (J10 prompt-cache + KV miss detection)

J10 complete: prompt-cache (KV) miss detection + reusable-token accounting, and the
merge gate now passes.

Task (from `.jgatefail.txt`): the branch had a MERGE CONFLICT with manus-parity. Ran
`git merge manus-parity`, resolved every conflict keeping BOTH sides (never dropping
either), got all gates green, and recorded the result here.

### Merge gate (the failure that was fixed)
Two files conflicted on the first merge:
- `src/agent/events.ts`: kept the incoming `compaction` event with `blocked?: boolean`
  (parity) AND this branch's `cache_usage` event (J10). Both event kinds are in the
  union now.
- `packages/web/public/marketplace/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES`: kept BOTH jcode MIT notices.
  The J10 KV-miss-detection notice (HEAD) and the `bench/` adaptation notice (parity)
  each keep their own section, sharing one MIT License block. Neither notice was dropped.
Resolution committed as `6a6c3f5 Merge manus-parity (keep both sides) into jcode-j10`.

A typecheck failure surfaced by that merge was fixed (not worked around): the
`compression` literal in `src/agent/__tests__/cacheUsageAccounting.test.ts` was missing
the new `bufferTokens` / `reattachFiles` / `reattachFileChars` fields. Added them to
match the config type (same values as `contextCompressor.test.ts`). The test assertions
are unchanged.

manus-parity advanced three times while this gate ran (14 commits, then 7 more, then
again). Each new tip was merged and re-verified:
- `5fc32c4 Merge branch 'manus-parity' into khamis1992/jcode-j10`
- `4e8ff1e Merge branch 'manus-parity' into khamis1992/jcode-j10` (current tip)
All three merges were conflict-free after the first resolution, and the branch is now
0 commits behind manus-parity.

### What J10 delivers
- `src/agent/kvCacheMonitor.ts`: normalizes provider usage into
  `{ promptTokens, cachedTokens, cacheWriteTokens? }`.
  - `parseOpenAiUsage`: `prompt_tokens` + `prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens`
    (plus the legacy top-level `cached_tokens`), clamped so cached never exceeds prompt.
  - `parseAnthropicUsage`: `input_tokens` + `cache_read_input_tokens` +
    `cache_creation_input_tokens`.
  - `parseOllamaUsage`: Ollama prompt-eval counters (also accepts the nested
    `cached_tokens.tokens` shape).
  - Miss-reason detection: cached ratio collapses after compaction, idle gap past the
    cache TTL, and model switch each produce a distinct reason.
- `src/ollama.ts`: provider usage types carry the cache fields.
- `src/agent/events.ts` + `src/protocol/{events,types}.ts` + `packages/shared/src/socket.ts`:
  the `cache_usage` event/counter wire format.
- `packages/web/src/components/chat/CacheUsageRow.tsx`: the small chat notice, wired into
  `EventList.tsx`, with `en`/`ar` strings.
- `src/agent/loop.ts`: reusable-token accounting on the per-step usage re-sum, so a
  prompt-cache read is no longer dropped when usage is recomputed (fix `a12d0e0`).

### Gates (all run from the worktree root, on merged tip `4e8ff1e`)
