## Incoming manus-parity report (V13 quick-edit route)

V13 (quick-edit route) is complete, and the merge gate passes.

### What V13 delivers (commit 639a92c)
- `src/agent/quickEdit.ts`: conservative classifier. Measured scope wins (text-only or
  pure reorder, within limits) -> fast model; behavioural / structural / file-boundary /
  oversized / multi-file / ambiguous -> base model. Short instructions classified by
  narrow-vs-big patterns in English and Arabic; ambiguous or long instructions stay on
  the base model.
- `resolveQuickEditModel` uses the configured fast tier (`fallbackModel`), falling back
  to the base model when it is unset; `planQuickEditRoute` adds a minimal targeted-edit
  instruction (English + Arabic) only for the quick route.
- `planTargetedDiff(before, after)` turns a before/after pair into line-anchored patches
  via the now-exported `diffLines`/`DiffSummary`/`DiffHunk`.
- Arabic/RTL: narrow-edit instructions are recognised in Arabic, `hasRtlScript` detects
  RTL script, and a targeted patch preserves Arabic text exactly (covered by tests).
- `src/agent/loop.ts` and `src/agent/orchestrator.ts`: optional per-run `model` override
  so the quick-edit route can actually run on the fast model; `src/index.ts` passes it
  through.

### Gates
- `npx tsc --noEmit` -> clean
- `npm run build:server` -> dist/server.cjs built, pdf worker copied
- `(cd packages/web && npx next build)` -> compiled successfully, 25/25 static pages
- `node --import tsx --test src/agent/__tests__/*.test.ts src/server/__tests__/*.test.ts` -> 527 pass, 0 fail
- `node --import tsx --test src/tools/__tests__/*.test.ts` -> 543 pass, 0 fail

Working tree is clean; no existing test was weakened.

