Fixed the interaction the resolution exposed: parity's coding router now intercepts
orchestrator worker calls, so a worker prompt that trips isCodingTurn escaped the
injected fake client and hit the real provider chain (this is what made
loopHooks.test.ts and orchestratorHooks.test.ts fail with provider HTTP 404s).
src/agent/orchestrator.ts now forwards createProviderClient / cooldownStore / env /
onCodingRoute into the child runAgent call, and orchestratorHooks.test.ts injects a
coder fake plus an in-memory cooldown store and empty failover so routing stays
hermetic. No test was weakened or deleted; the hooks.test.ts union is additive.

