Pre-existing, not a regression: `npm run check:orchestrator` exits 1 with no verdict on
BOTH this tip and the manus-parity baseline (a5d0cf3), with the identical crash
(runFinalRepair -> all providers failed/cooled -> longcat:cloud HTTP 404). Cause is the
smoke harness's testCfg() calling loadConfig() without overriding coding/failover, so
real defaults apply and a worker coding turn escapes to the network. It is an upstream
harness defect, not introduced by this merge; it was not masked or altered here.

Note: src/agent/masterPromptText.ts shows as "modified" after a test run because
src/tools/__tests__/promptwire.test.ts imports src/scripts/gen-master-prompt.ts, which
calls main() at import time and rewrites the file with LF endings. Content is
byte-identical to the committed version (git diff empty); only line-ending noise under
core.autocrlf=true. Restored with git checkout, working tree clean.
